-- title:
--   Theorem 4.2, p. 10 — feasible limit points of Algorithm 1 satisfying the generalized Łojasiewicz inequality for ½‖Π_𝒦°(G(x))‖² are CAKKT points
-- statement:
--   Consider the nonlinear conic program (NCP): minimize $f(x)$ subject to $G(x)\in\mathcal K$, with $f:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ and $G:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb E$ continuously differentiable and $\mathcal K$ a nonempty closed convex cone in a finite-dimensional real inner product space $\mathbb E$. Let $\{x^k\}_{k\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence generated by Algorithm 1, the augmented Lagrangian method, and let $\bar x$ be a feasible limit point of $\{x^k\}$. If $\bar x$ satisfies the generalized Łojasiewicz inequality (28) for
--   $$\Psi(x)=\tfrac12\big\|\Pi_{\mathcal K^\circ}(G(x))\big\|^2,$$
--   then $\bar x$ satisfies CAKKT (Definition 3.3): there are sequences $x^k\to\bar x$ and $\Lambda^k\in\mathcal K^\circ$ with $\nabla f(x^k)+DG(x^k)^*\Lambda^k\to0$, $\langle\Lambda^k,\Pi_{\mathcal K}(G(x^k))\rangle\to0$ and $\langle\Lambda^k,\Pi_{\mathcal K^\circ}(G(x^k))\rangle\to0$.
--
--   CAKKT asks, on top of AGP, for the complementarity limit (18) on the same sequences. The theorem thus refines the convergence theory of the augmented Lagrangian method beyond Theorem 4.1, without any constraint qualification; for nonlinear semidefinite programming it improves the earlier result that such methods generate TAKKT sequences under the same inequality.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "Limit point" is a cluster point (`MapClusterPt`) of $\{x^k\}$. The three limits of CAKKT hold for one and the same pair of sequences. Algorithm 1 is the run predicate `IsALRun`, with every free choice of the algorithm left free.
-- source:
--   Andreani, Gómez, Haeser, Mito & Ramos, On Optimality Conditions for Nonlinear Conic Programming, author's manuscript (revised 2021-04-20; Math. Oper. Res. doi:10.1287/moor.2021.1203), Theorem 4.2, p. 10

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MoreauProx_Decomposition_Cones
import Definitions.Def_NCPSeqOpt_AugLag_Setting

namespace NCPSeqOpt.AugLag

open MoreauProx.Decomposition
open scoped InnerProductSpace
open Filter Topology

theorem theorem_4_2 {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {n : ℕ}
    (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 1 f)
    (G : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → E) (hG : ContDiff ℝ 1 G)
    (K : Set E) (hK : IsClosedConvexCone K)
    (ε : ℕ → ℝ) (B : Set E) (τ σ ρ₀ : ℝ) (x : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (Λhat : ℕ → E) (ρ : ℕ → ℝ) (hrun : IsALRun f G K ε B τ σ ρ₀ x Λhat ρ)
    (xbar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (hfeas : G xbar ∈ K) (hlim : MapClusterPt xbar atTop x)
    (hL : GenLojasiewicz (Psi K G) xbar) :
    IsCAKKT f G K xbar := by sorry

end NCPSeqOpt.AugLag
